  "summary": "Hosted ComfyUI service that rents a private machine with one GPU by the second for image and video workflows. Its pricing page lists an hourly pay-as-you-go price per machine size; the figure here is that price in US dollars as printed, for the whole machine (the GPU with the vCPUs and memory shown beside it). Machine sizes that name two possible cards are not listed, and the lower Pro rates need a monthly subscription. The page says nothing about VAT.",
  "notes": "Static GPU Machine table (GPU Machine, Pay as You Go, Pro), found by its first header; Pay as You Go column only (Pro needs a monthly subscription). Only machines naming one card are read - \"T4, A4000\", \"A10G, A5000\", \"L40S, L40\" name two and are reported; the VRAM figure must equal the mapped card's memory. The training \"special rate\" table is another product, not read. Scope instance (the machine with its vCPUs and RAM); instance = tier name; on_demand, per_gpu, region null; USD as printed, no word on VAT",
